[size=4][b]Morrow Winds[/b][/size]

[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/51734]Morrow Winds[/url] is a separate music pack supported by the 03 playlists. Install it separately, then enable the playlists for its cities, regions, interiors, and Dagoth Ur combat music. Its music is found under [font=Courier New]Music/MS/cell[/font], [font=Courier New]Music/MS/interior[/font], [font=Courier New]Music/MS/region[/font], and [font=Courier New]Music/MS/combat/Dagoth Ur[/font].

[size=4][b]CaptainCreepy Music Pack[/b][/size]

[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/51769]CaptainCreepy Music Pack[/url] is also a separate music pack supported by the 03 playlists. Its core music is found under [font=Courier New]Music/MS/cell[/font], [font=Courier New]Music/MS/interior/Daedric[/font], and [font=Courier New]Music/MS/region[/font]. Its optional [font=Courier New]01 TAVERNS[/font] module is supported by [font=Courier New]10 Inns and Taverns[/font]. Its optional [font=Courier New]02 VAMPIRE COMBAT[/font] module is supported by [font=Courier New]Music/MS/combat/Vampire[/font] through [font=Courier New]Muse Vampire.lua[/font].

[color=#d4d4d8][b]General rule:[/b] if a playlist has no matching tracks, S3maphore ignores it. You can install playlist modules ahead of time without filling your game with errors.[/color]

[heading][center][color=#b48cff]COMPATIBILITY[/color][/center][/heading]

Music mods that add or replace tracks in the normal [font=Courier New]Music/Explore[/font], [font=Courier New]Music/Battle[/font], or [font=Courier New]Music/Special[/font] folders are compatible with S3maphore automatically.

Playlist-only modules are different: they point at specific folders and need matching tracks. Dynamic Music and MUSE soundbanks are handled on a case-by-case basis through the included playlist modules.

Some mods use MWScript to play music directly. S3maphore does not change that interface.

[heading][center][color=#b48cff]USAGE[/color][/center][/heading]

[size=4][b]Adding your own music[/b][/size]

Most S3maphore playlists are folder-based. The empty [font=Courier New]Music[/font] folders included with each playlist module are intentional drop zones for your own tracks. You do not need to edit Lua to add music.

For example, a track placed here will be available to the Hlaalu playlist:

[code]03 Muse Expansion Playlists/Music/ms/cell/hlaalu/my-hlaalu-track.mp3[/code]

You can also place the same [font=Courier New]Music/...[/font] path in a separate OpenMW data directory. S3maphore searches the OpenMW virtual file system, so your music does not need to be copied into the S3maphore folder. This is also how playlist-only modules use tracks supplied by other music mods.

Some playlists use an explicit list of tracks instead of accepting everything in a folder. The folder list for each module tells you which paths it uses. If a playlist cannot be toggled in the settings menu, S3maphore did not find any of its registered tracks.

[list]
[*][b]F8[/b] — skip the current track.[/*]
[*][b]Shift+F8[/b] — toggle S3maphore music on or off.[/*]
[*]Use the S3maphore settings menu to enable debug messages, show track and playlist names, enable or disable combat music, control silence tracks, and decide whether a new playlist should finish the previous track.[/*]
[*]The settings menu also lets you permanently enable or disable individual registered playlists.[/*]
[/list]

If a playlist cannot be toggled, S3maphore did not find any of its registered tracks. Check that the source music mod is installed as an OpenMW data directory and that the correct playlist module is enabled.

[heading][center][color=#b48cff]TROUBLESHOOTING[/color][/center][/heading]

[size=4][b]No music plays[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]1.[/b] Confirm that [font=Courier New]00 Core[/font] is enabled.[/*]
[*][b]2.[/b] Confirm that [font=Courier New]S3maphore.esp[/font] is enabled in OpenMW's content list.[/*]
[*][b]3.[/b] Confirm that H3lp Yours3lf is installed.[/*]
[*][b]4.[/b] If you enabled an optional module, install the music mod it expects.[/*]
[*][b]5.[/b] Do not flatten S3maphore's numbered data directories into [font=Courier New]Data Files[/font]. Add them separately to OpenMW.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]An optional playlist does nothing[/b][/size]

That is normally expected when its music is missing. A playlist-only module is intentionally silent until it finds tracks in its registered folder.

[size=4][b]You need more information[/b][/size]

Enable S3maphore debug messages and inspect [font=Courier New]openmw.log[/font]. S3maphore log messages begin with [font=Courier New][ S3MAPHORE ][/font].

[heading][center][color=#b48cff]FOR PLAYLIST AUTHORS[/color][/center][/heading]

S3maphore playlist files are Lua modules. A playlist can use built-in rules or combine them into entirely new conditions. The full documentation covers playlist creation, priorities, rules, events, localization, and the public interface:

[center][url=https://dreamweave-mp.github.io/S3ctors-S3cret-St4sh/s3maphore/modder-docs/][b]Read the S3maphore playlist-author documentation[/b][/url][/center]

